/// Plugin messaging between users in the same channel (FR-6.17, FR-6.33 … FR-6.36).
///
/// Messages reach only the same plugin id from the same source (official, the same third-party
/// repository, or developer) in Mumcord clients in the user's current channel on the current
/// server. The receiver learns the sender from the Mumble session that sent the message, never
/// from the payload. Incoming messages arrive as the `peer-message` event.
interface peers {
  use types.{error, peer, session};

  /// Who a message goes to.
  variant target {
    /// Everyone in the user's current channel who runs this plugin.
    channel,
    /// One user in the user's current channel.
    direct(session),
  }

  /// Sends one message. Needs `peers.messages`.
  ///
  /// `kind` is the plugin's own message type (byte 2 of the wire envelope). `payload` is at most
  /// 997 bytes and at most the manifest's `messaging.max_payload`.
  /// Rate limits: per plugin 1 message per 2 s sustained (burst 3), or 4 per second during a game
  /// burst; all plugins together 1 per second (burst 5). Mumcord's own features go first; a
  /// message that cannot be sent within 10 s is dropped and counted in Diagnostics.
  /// With visibility 'Friends' only friends receive it.
  /// Errors: `not-permitted`, `too-large`, `rate-limited`, `no-recipients` (not connected, server
  /// without plugin data, or nobody in the channel runs this plugin), `hidden` (visibility
  /// 'Nobody', or a direct target who is not a friend under 'Friends').
  send: func(to: target, kind: u8, payload: list<u8>) -> result<_, error>;

  /// Raises this plugin's send rate to 4 messages per second for the next 10 s, for real-time
  /// games. At most once per minute per plugin, and only one plugin at a time.
  /// Errors: `not-permitted` (no `peers.messages`), `rate-limited`.
  start-game-burst: func() -> result<_, error>;

  /// Snapshot of the users in the user's current channel, including the user themselves (first
  /// entry). Empty while disconnected. Needs `events.presence`. Errors: `not-permitted`.
  presence: func() -> result<list<peer>, error>;
}
